-- title:
--   At most one minimal prime of the H₁ moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$, admitting a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) (the kernel of the reduction of unit groups supplied by the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, and an element $j$ of $K$ equal in $L((T))$ to the base-changed $j$-series, assumed nonzero. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(q)$, acting on both $A$ and $K$ compatibly, with $A$ finite over $A_0$, generated as an $A_0$-algebra by an element $\zeta_A$ whose image in $L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity; assume $A_0$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity and that $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A_0$. Assume further: the three functoriality riders saying that over every $A_0$-algebra a variable change preserves $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-points (a point with $x_P = x_Q$, $y_P = y_Q$ on the curve and $(\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x_P) = 0$), preserves the $\Gamma_0$-prime-power cyclic-kernel conditions via `kernelVariableChangeDeg`, and preserves divisibility of `inLineMulPoly`; a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the projective Weierstrass models with unit discriminant which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ of raw Drinfeld pairs for $q$ which is a section transport; and the two graded-ring riders producing, for every variable change and every coefficient map, a homomorphism of the graded coordinate rings of the projective models respecting the irrelevant ideals and implementing the variable change, respectively the coefficient map. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package over $A_0$ for the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓ M' q …` — the rigidified data whose level structures combine the $\Gamma_0$-prime-power polynomials for $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point and a Drinfeld $q$-basis, subject to the linking condition at $\ell$ — with representing algebra $P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, and let $x$ be a point of the datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant equals, in $L((T))$, the $q$-fold reindexing [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) of the $j$-series. Then the set of minimal primes over the zero ideal of $P_0.B_0$ is finite and has cardinality at most $1$.
--
--   This is the integral-structure step for the $H_1$-level moduli ring over the $q$-unramified base $A_0$: the count of minimal primes upstairs over $A = A_0[\zeta_q]$ (where the Tate point forces $q-1$ components) is transferred down through the adjunction of $\zeta_q$, leaving at most one minimal prime over $A_0$. It feeds the statement that $P_0.B_0$ is a domain, used in the irreducibility analysis of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with the given level subgroup.
-- source:
